# Regenerate with: python tools/apply-sdk.py
#
# PocketJS retained UI core on ArtInChip D13x / Luban-Lite.
#
# Gate 1 scope: the node tree, style, taffy layout, text, animation and
# draw-list emission that a host drives through pocketjs_ui_core_*. No QuickJS,
# no framebuffer, no GE - those are later gates.

menuconfig LPKG_USING_POCKETJS_UI_CORE
    bool "PocketJS retained UI core"
    default n
    depends on LPKG_USING_POCKETJS
    help
      Builds the retained UI core for the ArtInChip D13x.

      The Rust half is delivered as a prebuilt staticlib,
      libpocketjs_rtthread_ui_core.a, which is deliberately NOT committed.
      Produce it from the PocketJS repository before building:

        python hosts/rt-thread/ports/artinchip-d13x/tools/build-firmware.py

      If the archive is absent the SConscript fails with instructions rather
      than silently linking a firmware without a UI core.

      This component depends on the `pocketjs` package because that package
      owns the host seam the UI core allocates through (pjs_host_alloc /
      pjs_host_free) and logs through (pjs_host_log). Enabling this without
      `pocketjs` would leave those undefined at link time.

if LPKG_USING_POCKETJS_UI_CORE

config LPKG_POCKETJS_UI_CORE_DEMO
    bool "Expose the pjs_ui_core MSH command"
    default y
    help
      Registers a command that drives the UI core from the prompt: create and
      destroy an instance, build a small node tree, tick, draw, and prove the
      frame borrow contract by showing that a stale view is rejected.

      Turning this off builds the UI core without the self-test, which is what
      a shipping configuration eventually wants.

config LPKG_POCKETJS_UI_CORE_AUTORUN
    bool "Run the UI core self-test once at boot"
    default y
    help
      Makes the Gate 1 evidence appear on the console without an operator at
      the prompt. Useful on bring-up hardware with no interactive terminal.

endif
